  "section_notes": "The final text is signed only by Northwind, and Halcyon's red line HC-1 is not met because per-model results go only to the regulator, not to customers. S2 is the most consequential weakening: it allows models above 5% to keep selling indefinitely under regulator safeguards, which benefits Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2%. S5 retains an 8-per-100k review trigger but leaves recall to regulator discretion, which benefits Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. S1 (72-hour reporting for all incidents) is reasonably strong, and S3 (6-year retrofit) and S4 (36-month suppression) sit at the edges of acceptable."
